# ── SECRETS — NEVER COMMIT ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Hard-block. Anything that could hold a key, a token, or a credential.
.credentials.json
*.credentials.json
credentials.json
*.env
.env
.env.*
settings.local.json
*.local.json
*secret*
*token*
*apikey*
*api-key*
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa
id_ed25519
*service-account*.json
gcp-*.json
# Shopify / Stripe / OpenAI / Anthropic / GitHub token shapes
shpat_*
shpss_*
sk-*
rk_*
ghp_*
gho_*

# ── EXCEPTIONS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Legit repo files whose NAME matches a pattern above
# (e.g. "secret-scan.yml" contains "secret" but it's our workflow).
#
# This block is not cosmetic: without it, two hook scripts that settings.json REFERENCES
# were silently excluded from the repo, so a fresh clone installed a settings.json
# pointing at files that did not exist. A name-based secret filter needs the list of what
# only LOOKS like a secret - the same lesson as PITFALLS.md -> secret leak, mirrored.
# Each line below has been read; none contains a credential.
!.github/workflows/secret-scan.yml
!scripts/shop-token-identity-block.ps1
!scripts/shopify-token-check.ps1
!shops/scaffold/scripts/get-token.sh
!shops/scaffold/.claude/settings.local.json
!shops/scaffold/.secrets/*.example
!skills/video-use/.env.example
# Vendored third-party source whose FILE NAMES contain "token"/"secret" (they implement
# token registries and secret-sink tests; they hold no value of either).
!skills/gstack/**/*token*
!skills/gstack/**/*secret*
# The course platform's own chapter index. It is called *token*.json because it carries
# Mux signed playback tokens (short-lived JWTs, the ones in this copy expired in 2026-06)
# next to the module titles and video ids - it is the table of contents of the library,
# not a credential of ours. Named here on purpose: the whole point of this block is that
# nothing gets dropped by its FILENAME without someone deciding it.
!formations/**/ecom_tokens.json

# ── SENSITIVE FOLDERS ───────────────────────────────────────────────
.aws/
.ssh/
.gnupg/

# ── LOCAL / RUNTIME NOISE ───────────────────────────────────────────
history.jsonl
*.log
*.bak
*.bak-*
cache/
debug/
shell-snapshots/
session-env/
sessions/
todos/
file-history/
paste-cache/
projects/
node_modules/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
# Kept: the transcription run log of the live replays - it is how the .md transcripts in
# formations/ were produced (whisper large-v3, cuda/fp16), not runtime noise. This line
# has to sit AFTER *.log above: in .gitignore the LAST matching rule wins, so putting the
# negation up in the EXCEPTIONS block silently did nothing.
!formations/**/*.log

# -- LOCAL, MACHINE-SPECIFIC CONFIG (never commit: names your real folders) ----
protected-zones.json
shops-registry.json
shops-registry.md
.asset-delete-unlock
.pitfall-tips-cache.json

# -- AUDIO ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# formations/ used to be ignored wholesale, back when this repo was public. It is
# private now and the training libraries ship with it - EXCEPT the audio: GitHub refuses
# any single file over 100 MB and one replay is 104.7 MB, so a plain push cannot even
# succeed. Every one of the 82 files is inventoried in formations/AUDIO-MANIFEST.md and
# formations/scripts/add-audio.ps1 puts them back. Delete these five lines only together
# with turning on Git LFS, or the next push will fail on the first big file.
*.mp3
*.m4a
*.wav
*.mp4
*.mov
